cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: CORR-Vars
abstract: >-
  CORR-Vars is a Python library for building reproducible clinical study cohorts
  from intensive-care and hospital data sources. A cohort is assembled at an
  explicit observation level — patient, hospital stay, ICU stay or procedure —
  and static and time-series variables are added to it from one or more
  pluggable data sources. Inclusion and exclusion steps are tracked as they are
  applied, so the resulting flowchart and baseline tables are generated from the
  cohort itself rather than maintained alongside it. Variable definitions are not
  bundled with the software: they are fetched per concept and per source from the
  CORR Concepts API, which records the exact definition version served, allowing
  a whole cohort — including every derived variable's dependencies — to be frozen
  to a date and rebuilt later. Results export to Stata, CSV, Excel and LaTeX or
  Markdown baseline tables.
type: software
